WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.480
<b>Tanukidanisan Fudo-in Temple</b>

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.840
<i>Once upon a time,</i>

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.080
<i>in the Tanukidani Fudo Forest
in Ichijoji, Sakyo Ward,</i>

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.590
<i>there lived a tanuki who was
young and fresh as a peach</i>

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>and carried herself light
as a mountain hermit.</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.280
<i>All the little tanuki in the
neighborhood were awed,</i>

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.700
<i>and in reverence, they called her
"Tousen the Step Climber."</i>

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.890
<i>One day, a group of mischievous boys,
inspired by the tsuchinoko boom of the time,</i>

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.060
<i>who wrought havoc
on the nearby mountains appeared.</i>

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.240
<i>They called themselves the
"Tsuchinoko Expedition Squad."</i>

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.090
<i>It was then that the little tanuki
of Tanukidani Fudo</i>

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.310
<i>and the Tsuchinoko Expedition Squad</i>

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:40.470
<i>began their battle over the long
stone steps of the approach.</i>

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.430
<b>Fall Festival</b>

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.250
<i>Time passed...</i>

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.640
<i>And one day,</i>

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.430
<i>the captain of the Tsuchinoko
Expedition Squad who yelled,</i>

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.520
<i>"Out of the way, you little shrimp!"</i>

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.600
<i>who was named Shimogamo Soichiro—</i>

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.030
<i>in other words, our father—</i>

00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.400
<i>was bound to...</i>

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.770
<i>the tomboy who responded with,
"What'd you say, you jerk?!"</i>

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.040
<i>who needless to say is our mother.</i>

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>Were it not for this furry little love story,</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.110
<i>not a single tuft of fur would have
existed of the Shimogamo brothers.</i>

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:15.950
<i>What lay beyond the birth of the round,</i>

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.690
<i>little furballs was a furry story of love.</i>

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.380
<i>The Trick Magister, Shimogamo Soichiro,</i>

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.700
<i>dutifully split his great blood four ways.</i>

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:31.440
<i>I was born in the Tadasu Forest
as his third son.</i>

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.950
<i>But unfortunately,</i>

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.760
<i>it appears that we fell a bit short
of living up to our father's greatness.</i>

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.360
<i>And after his passing,</i>

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.700
<i>we, the Tadasu Forest Brothers,</i>

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.580
<i>were referred to as fools who failed to
inherit their distinguished father's blood.</i>

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:48.670
<i>However...</i>

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.440
<i>As a tanuki whose father's
"fool's blood" flows through my body,</i>

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.070
<i>how else could I live?</i>

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.180
<i>There is no path for me</i>

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.220
<i>other than that of a fool!</i>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.980
<b>Episode One
 The Nidaime's Homecoming</b>

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.390
So is this tsuchinoko thing
anything like a bamboo shoot?

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.420
Not in the least, Mother.

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:24.400
So it's just a weird little snake.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.500
I bet its flesh is all chewy.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.500
Definitely not tasty at all.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.800
Not at all!

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.000
Er, we aren't going to eat it.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.880
Come to think of it, Sou-san searched
for them when he was young, too.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.580
Honestly, I have no words.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.420
Weird little tanuki do get fixated
on weird little things.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:50.570
Stop chasing around something
as dubious as tsuchinoko.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.270
You should play shogi as well.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.770
Tsuchinoko were one
of Father's hobbies, too!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.640
Quit your yapping.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.940
I'm going to bring back the shogi tournament

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.250
that was put on hold
when Father went in a hot pot.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.830
The least you could do is help.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:03.720
What the heck?

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.530
You don't even play shogi.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.440
There are plenty of tanuki
who like to play shogi!

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.740
Becoming the Trick Magister

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.000
means that I should
always think of tanuki first.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.500
There you go again.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.250
This time I will definitely

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.890
become the Trick Magister!

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.900
Take care!

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.470
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.460
Yashiro,

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.450
I appoint you member number one
of the Tsuchinoko Expedition Squad.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.280
Yay.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.310
"Member number one" sounds cool.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.070
<b>Crossroads of the Six Realms</b>

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.570
So...

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.950
No one understands how cool tsuchinoko are.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.470
But you know, Yasaburo,

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.870
if I did find a tsuchinoko,

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.720
it means that I'm going
to be swallowed whole.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.330
Because, you know,
it's a snake, and I'm a frog.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.830
That's true.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.560
Which means

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.960
that I can't join the
Tsuchinoko Expedition Squad.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:05.120
Is Yashiro still working at the
Trick Denki Bran factory as an apprentice?

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.180
Yup.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.220
It <i>is</i> one of our family's
sources of steady income.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.790
Well, Nii-san, I'll be going now.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.730
See ya.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.940
Another boring day is 
about to come to an end.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.820
By the way, have you received
any letters from Benten-sama?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.200
And why would you want to know that?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.170
Why won't you tell me?

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.800
You talk too much.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.500
How is my correspondence with Benten
any business of yours?

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.790
I'm going to cross the sea.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.340
A cruise around the world?

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.150
What brought this on?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.850
Well, I'm bored.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:56.380
Yasaburo, make sure you
take care of Sensei for me.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.300
I might write you a letter if I feel like it.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.460
Benten...

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.120
Benten...

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:19.780
Good grief.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:21.630
Oh?

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.190
Carefully... Carefully...

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.590
Benten...

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:32.400
Oh, Benten...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.900
<b>I hate the rain – Benten</b>

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.900
<b>To my master
Near the edge of Kamigyo Ward, Kyoto City</b>

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.900
"I hate the rain."

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.400
<b>Bored – Benten</b>

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.400
<b>Master's apartment in 
Kamigyo Ward, Kyoto City</b>

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.560
"Bored."

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.150
<b>To my master in Kyoto</b>

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:46.150
Huh?

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.780
Wh-What the heck is this?

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:06.110
Nii-chan, it smells like spring.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.400
Hey, keep your eyes peeled.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.070
We don't know where they might be hiding.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.760
I wonder if tsuchinoko actually exist.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:17.690
The fact that we don't know if they exist
is what's so great about them.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:29.480
Yashiro, could you put even one percent

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.390
of that passion
into searching for tsuchinoko?

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:36.280
Nii-chan, "Genius is one percent inspiration,

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.580
ninety-nine percent perspiration."

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.100
Incorrect, Yashiro.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.360
Genius is one percent inspiration,

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.410
ninety-nine percent foolishness.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.590
Then when are you going to try?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.680
I will wait for my destiny.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:54.230
I don't think that's right.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.610
Why you shrimpy little Edison.

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.930
Shtop it, nii-hyan!

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:02.400
Look out!

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.870
Nii-chan, is this a tengu stone?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.310
Apparently, there are some
modern-looking tengu stones

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:19.600
falling through the skies lately.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.080
A tengu dropped it, right?

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:24.340
Let's take it home.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.380
Mother will be happy.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.260
Well...

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:31.520
As long as the tengu who dropped it
doesn't claim ownership,

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:34.350
there's probably no reason to return it.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.660
Nii-chan, won't we get yelled at if we search

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.490
for tsuchinoko this far out?

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:42.980
Who's going to yell at us?

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:46.360
Isn't this the Kurama tengu's territory?

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.800
Well, the whole area surrounding Nyoigatake

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.660
belongs to our Akadama-sensei.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:57.610
The Kurama tengu are just small fry
compared to Akadama-sensei.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.830
"Small fry," huh?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.620
S-So heavy...

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.890
Well, you've got quite the mouth on you.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:09.960
Where are you from, tanuki?

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:13.200
Oh, hello there, esteemed member
of the Kurama tengu.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.120
How are you doing this fine day?

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.620
Apparently, Kurama tengu are just small fry.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.580
I humbly stand before you

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.520
as the third son
of Shimogamo Soichiro, Yasaburo.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.030
And this is my little brother, Yashiro.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.890
Prestigious! Prestigious!

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.360
So you're Yasaburo from the Shimogamo family.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.620
Apparently, he's Benten-san's favorite.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:41.120
Can't say that I like him one bit.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.580
Now, then...

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:49.690
I wonder how far we can 
throw this little one.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:53.510
Let's take bets on whether he'll
make it over the Kamo River or not.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.260
What's the matter, Yasaburo?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:56.830
I beg your pardon,

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.490
but when my little brother is being bullied,

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.400
my seizures start acting up.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.480
"Seizures"?

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.900
What are seizures?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.460
You mustn't, esteemed Kurama tengu.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.230
Please stand back.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.240
Huh?

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:17.450
Stop, stop, Yasaburo!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.550
This is foolish!

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.830
Return to your normal form immediately!

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:22.830
Or else...

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.120
What's this?

00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:31.030
Oh?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.560
It's rare to see an elephant in Nyoigatake.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.390
Ah, so it was a tanuki's transformation?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.490
Splendid transformation.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:56.760
Hello, my good sirs.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:59.110
What might you be doing in these parts?

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.240
If it isn't Yakushibo's Nidaime!

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:05.720
Why have you come back now?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.950
I've seen everything that I needed to see.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.380
Is the leader of the
Kurama tengu doing well?

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.250
By the way,

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:15.130
I had sent my luggage here, but...

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.470
Oh, that?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.130
They were in the way, so we tossed them out.

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.200
Why would you do such a thing?

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.310
This mountain doesn't belong to you.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.600
You're a bit late, Nidaime.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:29.270
We've taken over Nyoigatake.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.110
Oh, I see.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:35.530
Understood.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.720
Well, aren't you rather cold.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.740
We kicked your father off this mountain.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.990
Are you ashamed of your actions?

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.530
Why would we be ashamed?

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.710
Then show more pride.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.070
You are almighty tengu, after all.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.740
Speaking of which, where is my father?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.330
Behind the Demachi shopping arcade.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:01.510
Dependent on tanuki
in a crummy little apartment.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.010
Then I'll finish him myself.

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.830
Well, my good sirs,

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.060
if you'll excuse me.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.730
He's just as annoying as ever.

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.180
Who would've thought he'd come back now?

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:20.320
Should we let the head family know?

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.450
Nii-chan, you're alive!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.290
Go tell Yaichiro that the Nidaime's returned.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.940
What are you going to do, Nii-chan?

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.500
I'm going to Demachiyanagi.

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.990
Come in.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.480
Welcome home, my son!

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.820
What happened in the past was all my fault.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.650
Will you forgive me?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.780
You reek of tanuki, Father.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.950
The tanuki come here all the time.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.300
I'm rather sick of them myself.

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.780
You say that,

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.270
but it is rather apparent
that you are fond of tanuki.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.370
What are you talking about, you fool?

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:25.220
Why else would you
grow a tail like a tanuki's?

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:29.950
Please forgive me! I'm sorry!

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:33.770
Aren't you the tanuki from a few moments ago?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.560
I am the third son of
Shimogamo Soichiro, Yasaburo.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.620
Where is my real father?

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.550
I sadly have no idea.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:45.830
Where could he have gone?

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.880
Tanuki are such admirable little creatures.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.450
Tanuki are indeed admirable.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:57.380
If there is anything that you need,
simply say the word.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.690
I'm sure there must be

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.380
some inconveniences
after being gone for so long.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.510
We must find your furniture as well.

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:07.000
Indeed.

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:11.780
It appears that those Kurama fools
tossed my belongings from Nyoigatake.

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.020
A suggestion, if you would.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.340
Would you kindly let me take care of them?

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.480
I would be very grateful.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.150
However, I cannot allow you to work for free.

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:28.680
Tengu are made to make tanuki work hard.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.280
Tengu are greater than tanuki, after all.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:35.700
I do not like being indebted
to others, Yasaburo-kun.

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:39.600
Also, I am not a tengu.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:42.800
Where should I deliver them?

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.040
I will be staying at a hotel
in Kawaramachi Oike.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:01.770
Benten...

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.850
Benten...

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:08.110
Yasaka-san, the Trick Magister,

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.200
wants to ask you about the Nidaime.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:18.830
<b>Yasaka Clinic
Proctology Department</b>

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:14.170
I'm not an expert on tengu.

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.760
Shut your mouth.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.570
Help your fellow tanuki for once.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:18.570
Oh.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:22.090
Yasaburo-chan and Yaichiro-san.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.290
Hey, Gyokuran-sensei.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:26.060
Oh, don't call me "sensei."

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.100
H-Hey, Gyokuran.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.380
What are you doing here, Sensei?

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:34.360
Well, there's going to be
an event at Nanzenji.

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:36.630
Oh, the shogi tournament.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:37.690
You're serious about that.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:41.980
It seems that we'll be able to revive
the shogi tournament, Gyokuran.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:48.110
<b>Hemorrhoids
If you're troubled by hemorrhoids,
 please make an appointment.
Yasaka Clinic</b>

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.190
I look forward to it.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:48.110
After that, it'll be your turn 
to become the Trick Magister.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.630
R-Right...

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:52.020
It's a comeback!

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.180
It's Kinkaku.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:55.710
And Ginkaku.

00:14:55.710 --> 00:15:00.690
Don't think you can become the Trick Magister
just because Father went away.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.960
Yup.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:10.590
<b>Reception</b>

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:04.170
And here come the idiot twins.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.810
How did you two become
such twisted little fools?

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.920
That's quite a thing to say.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:11.770
I've been deeply hurt.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:12.970
That hurt!

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Reception</b>

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.850
Just die from those wounds!

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:16.030
What did you say?

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:17.470
That's enough!

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:20.350
Kureichiro-niisan.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:25.450
I apologize for the trouble
that my idiot brothers have caused you.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:27.410
Kureichiro...

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.110
What brings you here today?

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.760
I came to talk to the Trick Magister

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.390
about the things that my father left behind.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:36.210
Did you work something out?

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:38.390
Yes, thank you.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.320
If you'll excuse us.

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:48.610
I'll be leaving now, too.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:49.940
See ya.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.010
<b>Heitaro's Examination and Reception Office</b>

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:52.640
Hey, there.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.420
Sorry for the trouble.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.390
Welcome to Trick Hawaii.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.660
So, Yasaburo...

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:03.400
Was that Nidaime the real Nidaime?

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.270
What do you mean?

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.810
It happened a hundred years ago.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.680
He and his father, Nyoigatake Yakushibo-sama,

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.810
held a fierce battle that lasted
three days and three nights.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.830
In the end, the Nidaime faced defeat

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.540
and left Japan.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:28.830
So there is a lot of strife

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:31.420
between Akadama-sensei and Nidaime.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.170
He's definitely a tengu.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:37.770
It's a bit strange that he
would deny that he is one, but...

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:41.430
He still seems to hold a grudge
against Akadama-sensei.

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:46.600
Well, I'm sure there'll be trouble
as soon as Benten-sama returns.

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.850
If we get involved in this,
our butts will catch on fire.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.940
Stop enjoying this, Yasaburo.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.480
It's fine.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:56.910
So, what do you think, Yaichiro-kun?

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.050
My brother is a fool.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:02.160
But I believe his judgment is correct.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.660
In the end, we're just tanuki.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.490
Haste makes waste.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.840
I'll stay true to the trick.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:16.680
Yasaburo, keep an eye
on any movements from the tengu.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:19.870
In return,

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:23.090
I would like to return
to the Nidaime the tengu stones

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:25.320
that the Kurama tengu scattered about.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:27.080
Can we do something about it?

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.080
All right.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.830
I'll let everyone know.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:38.210
By the way, does Akadama-sensei know
that the Nidaime has returned?

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:40.280
No, I don't think he knows.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:47.540
Sensei, it's me, Yasaburo.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.540
Kinkobo-sama.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:54.170
Yasaburo, are you hiding something from me?

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.870
What brought this on?

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:01.300
I have a lot of secrets, you know?

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.430
What is he up to?

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.390
He's at a hotel in Kawaramachi Oike.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.390
Take this to him.

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:11.400
<b>Duel</b>

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.400
Know that this is an honorable task.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:17.340
I, Shimogamo Yasaburo, am honored.

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.710
Hello, Yasaburo-kun.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:34.540
Thank you for your hard work.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.210
It was nothing.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.340
By the way, have you found a German air gun?

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.770
An air gun?

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:45.740
Does it shoot out something like furballs?

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.990
It's nothing that adorable.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.000
If you could find it immediately,
I would be grateful.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.070
There will be trouble
if it falls into the wrong hands.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.730
Here's your reward for today.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.120
Oh, that's not necessary.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:02.440
I don't like being indebted to people.

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.590
Well, I'm a tanuki.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.290
Allow me to rephrase.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.250
I don't like being indebted to tanuki.

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:11.750
To be honest,

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.840
I'm planning on asking
for a much bigger favor later.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.880
I don't think that gold coin will be enough.

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:19.640
And there you have it.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.900
I have a feeling I'll be
tricked if I'm not careful.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.590
If you're in a position to be tricked,

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:26.200
it can actually be quite wonderful.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.890
Well said.

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:31.270
Is that some tanuki wisdom?

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:36.230
Actually, Sensei asked me to deliver this.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:42.740
I might go. I might not.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:43.740
<b>Duel</b>

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.030
I would prefer for you
not to assume I will.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:08.360
Freely flying through the sky.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:11.620
That is what defines a tengu, but...

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:14.020
Good grief.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.860
Yakushibo!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.970
Fight with everything you have!

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:19.980
We'll pick up your bones for you.

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.930
And throw them into the Kamo River after!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.850
You stupid little mountain acorns...

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.760
One of these days, I'll throw you
into Lake Biwa.

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:45.340
Good evening, elderly gentleman.
What might you be doing in a place like this?

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.050
I'm expecting some company—

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:52.300
I am also expecting some company here.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.600
Who might you be waiting for?

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:57.030
Someone quite worthless, to be honest.

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:59.730
I'd rather not speak of them.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:03.260
Oh? Well, isn't that a coincidence.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:08.650
I'm waiting for someone
quite worthless as well.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:19.340
That fool was my son and my student
and foolishly decided to defy me.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:23.210
I thought I might drop him from here again.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:27.220
If you think you can, go ahead and try.

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.720
I shall.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:38.190
<i>Tengu have always peered down
at the world from the pinnacle of pride.</i>

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:43.610
<i>They are great because they are tengu,
and tengu because they are great.</i>

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:47.720
<i>"I am the only being of any significance
between Heaven and Earth."</i>

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:49.860
<i>This thought makes a tengu.</i>

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:55.600
<i>There is no way that this conflict
could ever be settled peacefully.</i>

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.390
Whoa, there. Don't you touch me, now.

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:35.510
You'll burn yourself on the flames of hell.

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:40.410
Let's set all the difficult stuff
aside and have some ramen.

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode  Two
The Conjurer Tenmanya</b>
